WEBVTT

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.090
Young Godai...

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.060
Young Godai?

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.630
Young Godai.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.450
M-Mr. Yotsuya!

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.410
Are you going out somewhere?

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:33.720
Young Godai...
Look at this.

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:17.630
Godai?

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.170
Godai!

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:21.760
Godai!

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:24.420
That wasn't my alarm...

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.380
Godai, I'm coming in.
Okay?

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:29.840
Open it. Open it!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.310
What a racket!

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:36.590
Move!

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:39.390
Do you realize what
time it is?!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.560
It...wasn't a dream...

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.600
Mr. Yotsuya gave it to you?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.140
Couldn't be.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:57.710
You're pullin' our
leg, right?

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.580
Did you and he have
a quarrel or something?

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.810
Is the egg his way of
getting revenge?

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:46.990
That's not it at all--

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.540
You don't ever want Yotsuya
to give you anything.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.200
That's right!

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.260
It's weird.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.830
Something's wrong.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.340
I...guess you're right.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.800
But...I haven't done
anything to him.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.840
It might be a trap.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.580
Something's definitely wrong.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.460
Is it dangerous?

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:21.120
I don't think it's a bomb.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:30.060
My heart skipped a beat--
Don't scare me like that!

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.040
Think about it, though.

00:05:33.140 --> 00:05:35.870
What if you got hungry
and ate it?

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:40.740
Young Godai, you ate
the egg I gave you...

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:43.780
Oh...my poor egg.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:46.130
But if you don't eat it...

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:51.090
Young Godai, you mean you won't
eat an egg I gave you?

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:54.240
Oh...my poor egg.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.090
That's right! He would!
That's exactly what he'd say!

00:05:58.180 --> 00:06:01.100
You sure got stuck with
with a can of worms...

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:06.340
Is it raw, or hard-boiled?

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.130
Does it make a difference?

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:14.410
Yes... One keeps much longer.

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:16.220
Oh, I see...

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:20.090
Either way, you might want
to put it in the fridge.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.310
You're right...

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:24.720
It's gone...

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.960
Oh no! It rolled off!

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.420
Move slowly...

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.430
We'll have big trouble
if it breaks.

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.740
I don't see it...

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:40.380
Where could it have gone?

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.380
Akemi's disappeared...

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:48.780
Akemi!

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.330
Akemi, what in the name of...!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:07.670
Darn...

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.030
Manager!

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.290
Did you find the egg?!

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.630
It's safe. Look!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.550
What's that you've
got there?

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.960
Oh, nothing.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.130
I know!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.090
W-What's the matter?

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.840
Could it be...?

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:52.040
A present for me?!

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:53.560
Oh my!

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.120
You shouldn't have, Godai!

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:57.510
It's not what you think...

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:59.950
This is the movie
I thought we'd see.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.390
Fish Eggs From Outer Space

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:07.720
What's the matter?
Not your kind of flick?

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:10.920
Hmm... An egg, huh?

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:14.040
I'm not sure if he
gave it to me

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.970
or if he just wanted me
to hold on to it.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:18.840
Flip that over.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.260
Just keep it warm.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.930
Yotsuya was keeping it
warm to hatch it.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:35.250
But he couldn't do it
so he wanted you to take his place.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:36.830
Couldn't be!

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.790
I wonder what'll hatch
from the egg?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:45.720
A chick, probably.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.590
Or a lizard.

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.120
What?

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.560
What if Mr. Yotsuya
laid the egg?

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:59.740
Maybe a tiny Yotsuya hatchling
will appear.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.210
Young Godai...

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.910
It's an egg, all right.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:38.220
Guess I'll just give it
back to him like this.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.330
I wouldn't want him
demanding the return

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:43.050
of an egg I'd already eaten.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.340
Manager...

00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:04.170
I guess Mr. Yotsuya hasn't
been home yet, has he?

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.920
Two beef bowls?
We'll be right over!

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:29.630
Ah...My heart pines for
The momentary joy of
A morsel of meat...

00:10:33.470 --> 00:10:36.910
If she's right, then we
can't put it in the fridge.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.970
We'd have to keep it
warm, instead.

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.850
Not that I believe her
though.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.590
First, let's determine if
it's raw or hard-boiled.

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.700
If it's hard-boiled
there's no problem.

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.890
But if it's raw, we'd
better keep it warm.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.130
Can you tell without
breaking it?

00:10:58.210 --> 00:10:59.130
Just a minute...

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:01.130
Now let me see...

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:04.740
It was in this book
I think...

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:06.670
Godai!

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.780
Let me see Mr. Yotsuya's egg.

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:11.600
Here it is. It's just
an ordinary egg.

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:13.300
Couldn't be.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:16.550
My mom was too
excited about it.

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.240
It's not the egg--

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.680
lt's my predicament
she's excited about.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:23.240
Let me borrow that!

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.550
Hey! Where're you
going with that!

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:29.300
Kentaro!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:30.680
Stop!

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:50.720
It wasn't in that book.
But I know I saw it somewhere.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.660
It was...raw.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:55.080
Was?

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.800
What's goin' on?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.800
So it was raw...

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:32.230
Yes...raw.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:35.050
Gosh, what'll I do now?!

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.380
Don't worry about it.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:41.030
When Mr. Yotsuya gets back,
I'll help explain what happened.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:42.200
I'd appreciate that.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:47.080
Some people can take it;
others can't.

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:48.740
That's the problem...

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.240
Hurray!
You all fell for it!

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.250
What're you talking about?

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.690
Look! I have the real egg
right here!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:03.380
K-K-Kentaro!!

00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:17.090
You don't have to tell me!

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:21.070
How many times have I told
you not to play with food!

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:22.240
Knucklehead!

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:23.610
I heard you already!

00:13:29.130 --> 00:13:30.790
Were you at the bath?

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:32.010
Yeah...

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.510
Sorry about all the
commotion earlier.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.860
That's okay.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.490
You brought it with
you to the bath?

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:43.570
I did. I felt it'd be safer
with me than in my room.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:45.050
You're right.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.160
They all mean well, but...

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:51.300
It's such a bother
because it's so fragile...

00:13:51.670 --> 00:13:53.690
It's only until Yotsuya
gets back.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:54.800
You're right...

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:56.910
You never know, though--

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:59.820
He might be watching
you from somewhere.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:07.250
S-Sorry! Couldn't you tell
I was just kidding?

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:23.410
The air is quiet...
Like insects into a flame...
The sound of water.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:27.340
All alone... The only
Fish in the pond.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.190
What's wrong?

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.940
Did Mr. Yotsuya show up
again last night?

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:48.420
The egg laid more eggs!

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.460
There might be even more
tomorrow morning!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:52.830
Don't be ridiculous!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.860
Wait a minute...

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.960
Kentaro's been up to
his tricks again.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:00.340
Here, look at this.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.800
A "circle-one" mark.

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:05.910
I forgot! I marked the egg
just in case, too!

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:06.750
What'd you use?

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.410
A circle and the character
for "yo."

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:14.440
Mrs. Ichinose, do you always
mark your eggs?

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.440
Doesn't everyone?

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:20.190
Really?

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.860
Circle-one... Circle-one...

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.660
This one... And this one, too!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.740
It's not here! They're all
marked circle-one!

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:35.630
Akemi!

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.190
You again...

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.360
Whew! It's not Yotsuya's egg!

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:00.940
You mean I took the wrong one?

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.260
Thank goodness!

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:05.590
Make sure you pay me
back for my eggs.

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:08.130
Then that means...

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.330
Hold it, Kentaro!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:13.670
Give me back the egg!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:14.580
No way!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.840
You're asking for
a hurting!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:17.920
I don't care!

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:21.380
I'll never help you with
your homework again!

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:22.790
Here, catch!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:30.400
Kentaro! Come back!

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.960
It's right here!

00:16:46.320 --> 00:16:50.260
You want to know how to tell
a raw egg from a hard-boiled one?

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:51.380
That's right.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:55.540
You're a good cook, so we
thought you might know.

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:58.050
I'm afraid I don't.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:16:59.080
I see...

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.260
But why?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:04.490
Because it might contain all
the world's misfortunes.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:06.450
We can't risk cracking it
open to see.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.660
That's a very dangerous egg.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:09.450
Right!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:13.500
Ms. Otonashi, dispose of it
before it breaks.

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.540
Godai's the one who's
got it.

00:17:15.620 --> 00:17:17.410
Godai does?

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:20.510
Then you should crack it
open immediately!

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:23.010
I figured you might
say that.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:30.580
If he asks for it back
give him a different one.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.950
If I gave him back
a different egg,

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.450
he'd be able to tell
right away.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.960
Do you really think
he would?

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.190
Do you have the guts
to find out?

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:42.730
Nope!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:53.110
Darn you!

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.750
Stop!
Kentaro!

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.540
Akemi?!

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.870
Shucks...
I was so close, too...

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:32.690
What? No way!

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:37.160
Please? You're the only
one I can ask to do this.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:39.550
No way... Not me!

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:43.920
No matter what?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:44.830
Nope!

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:46.940
I see...

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:17.090
Hello? Smiley Children's
help line...

00:19:17.160 --> 00:19:19.090
It's your turn, you're on the line.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:20.300
Hello?

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:26.630
Um... How do you tell a hard-
boiled egg from a raw one?

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.700
W-What is this place?

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.880
Is this where Yotsuya lives?

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:46.860
Nah, couldn't be!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.050
When'd you come in,
Sakamoto?

00:20:00.650 --> 00:20:02.480
Godai, I found out the answer!

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.490
What's with the two of you?

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.530
What'll we do?

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:22.360
What's going on?

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.230
Do you feel all right?

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.550
lt did taste a bit odd...

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:30.200
Godai, do you keep
any stomach medicine?

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:33.800
Did I just eat something terrible?

00:20:36.950 --> 00:20:40.700
Sometimes, ignorance is bliss.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.150
Hey! What's going on?
Tell me!

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:44.780
Friends tell friends, right?!

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.990
Manager!

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.780
It was hard-boiled.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:56.370
Yes, it was hard-boiled!
So what about it?!

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:01.900
At the tone, the time will
be 4:35 and 20 seconds.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:09.400
At the tone, the time will
be 4:35 and 30 seconds.

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:12.590
Think it'll work?

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:17.080
Yotsuya will know it
isn't his egg.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.950
I'd have to agree. He's pretty
sharp when it comes to food.

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:23.320
If this doesn't work
nothing's really changed.

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:26.010
Right now, we've got to
boil this egg.

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:30.230
Hey Godai! Will you tell
me what's going on?

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.530
Keep quiet and rest!

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:34.530
I don't get it...

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:37.660
Manager, I think we should
turn up the heat.

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:38.830
I think you're right.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:43.580
Now if we can just fool
Yotsuya...

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:06.260
Godai!

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:15.510
Hot!

00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:43.540
Young Godai!

00:22:44.010 --> 00:22:44.900
Y-Yes?

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:49.530
The heat's too high.

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:57.380
You mean that's it?

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:01.050
Make sure you replace
my eggs.

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:08.950
Hey Godai!
What the hell's going on?

00:23:09.040 --> 00:23:12.030
What was that egg
I just ate!

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.230
Tell me, Godai!

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.070
Godai!

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:26.130
It hurts...

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.050
My stomach!

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:28.710
G-Godai!

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:32.800
That's what you get for
eating Mr. Yotsuya's egg!

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:35.710
How was I to know?

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:41.880
Under the moonlight,
A friend cries in pain profound.

00:23:41.960 --> 00:23:44.920
He never should have eaten
The egg I just Found.

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.000
"This card she sent
remains a riddle..."

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:57.280
What card was Soichiro
referring to in his diary?

00:23:57.350 --> 00:24:01.540
Next: "The Case of the Shocking Diary--
My Husband had a Sweethearrt!?!"

00:24:01.620 --> 00:24:05.310
I don't recall ever sending
such a card...
